From: Production Enhancement <kernel@t100.local>
Date: Sat, 15 Feb 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH v2] media: i2c: mt9m114: Add production low-light with AtomISP fixes

This patch adds production-grade low-light performance improvements to the
MT9M114 sensor driver for Bay Trail (Asus T100) devices, with explicit
handling for AtomISP compatibility issues identified in real-world testing.

Key improvements:

1. Dynamic VTS (Vertical Total Size) adjustment - allows exposure time to
   exceed the standard frame interval by dropping FPS, crucial for low-light
   
2. 5x5 Exposure Metering Grid with preset patterns - weighted exposure zones
   with easy-to-use presets (center, uniform, backlit, spot)
   
3. AE Config Speed register (0x31AC) - enables fast AE response in dark scenes

4. Shadow Register (GROUP_HOLD) support - prevents "rolling shutter" artifacts
   when updating VTS and exposure atomically (register 0x8404)

5. Manual AE mode enforcement - disables sensor's internal auto-exposure when
   V4L2 manual controls are used, preventing hardware/software conflicts

6. AtomISP streaming guard - warns about framerate changes during streaming
   that may require ISP pipeline restart

The android-ia vendor kernel had these features but they were lost in the
mainline rewrite. This restores that functionality for production use with
additional safety mechanisms for the AtomISP CSS firmware.

Signed-off-by: Production Enhancement <kernel@t100.local>
